# =============================================================================
# ci-baselines.env — canonical CI ratchet baselines. SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH.
# =============================================================================
# Shell-sourceable (`. scripts/ci-baselines.env`) and parsed by
# scripts/check-ci-baselines.mjs, which fails the build if any other file
# declares one of these values and disagrees.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# These three numbers were duplicated across five places, and on 2026-08-09 no
# two of them agreed. Measured against origin/master (6e3018360) the real
# values were 186 / 0 / 78, while the declarations said:
#
#   scripts/ci-local.sh (header comment)   170 /  0 / 72   stale
#   scripts/ci-local.sh (enforced values)  185 /  0 / 78   one BELOW reality,
#                                                          so Gate 1 was red on
#                                                          a pristine master
#   .claude/commands/auto-improve.md      3790 / 77 / 91   ~20x too loose; the
#                                                          77 is the silent-catch
#                                                          count mistranscribed
#                                                          as a lint-error count
#   scripts/deploy-local-main.sh          3825 / 77 /  -   the PRODUCTION deploy
#                                                          gate, effectively inert
#   .github/workflows/ci.yml              3765 /  - /  -   the gate that actually
#                                                          blocks PRs
#
# A ratchet that nobody can state the value of is not a ratchet. Change a
# number here and everywhere else follows; there is nowhere else to change it.
#
# Rules
# -----
#   - Ratchet DOWN as issues are fixed. Never up without provenance below.
#   - Every change appends a dated line to the log: what moved, by how much,
#     and the evidence that it was pre-existing rather than PR-introduced.
#   - Verify on a CLEAN worktree of origin/master, never in the main checkout.
#
# Provenance log
# --------------
# 2026-04-29: 170→180 warnings, 72→74 catches — matched pre-existing master state (verified via git stash; not PR-introduced).
# 2026-05-08: 180→183 warnings — pre-existing master regressions from PRs #1554/#1556 that landed without bumping the baseline.
# 2026-05-19: 74→75 catches — olt-report/reporting.ts + wa-monitor-sync-sharepoint*.ts carried untracked pre-existing silent catches.
# 2026-05-20: 183→185 warnings — P3 scoped-snag-reports test files using the established withAuth mock pattern, plus one react-refresh warning.
# 2026-05-21: 75→76 catches — origin/master already at 76 (olt-report/reporting.ts:166 date-parse fallback).
# 2026-05-25: held at 185 — master emitted 186 (SerialLifecyclePanel.tsx react-refresh). Fixed at source instead of raising: the pure fn moved to serialLifecycle.utils.ts.
# 2026-07-24: 76→77 catches — origin/master already at 77 (communications/whatsapp/cloud-webhook.ts, PR #2239).
# 2026-07-25: 77→78 catches — origin/master already at 78; verified twice independently on clean checkouts.
# 2026-08-09: 185→186 warnings — origin/master (6e3018360) emits 186; the 185 baseline was below reality, so `npm run ci:quick` Gate 1 failed on an untouched master checkout. The extra warning is react-refresh/only-export-components on src/modules/fleet/components/FleetMapLegend.tsx, which exports RING_COLOUR and ORDER alongside the component. Its only non-component consumer is its own test file, so the 2026-05-25 fix-at-source treatment applies cleanly — deliberately left to a separate PR rather than folded into this tooling change. FOLLOW-UP: move RING_COLOUR/ORDER to FleetMapLegend.utils.ts and ratchet back to 185.
# 2026-08-09: NEW pages/ baselines at 1115 warnings / 0 errors. `npm run lint` is `eslint src` only, so pages/ — 1,623 files including every API route — was never linted at all except for no-silent-catch via Gate 2. Measured on a clean worktree of origin/master (bec3c03ef): 0 errors, 1115 warnings. The 27 errors that were there first (17 ban-ts-comment, 9 unused disable directives, 1 disable naming an unloaded rule) were cleared by PR #2416 so the gate could start at zero — ESLint exits non-zero on any error regardless of --max-warnings.
# 2026-08-22: NEW silent-catch baselines for src/ (1192) and pages/ outside pages/api (174). `no-silent-catch` is declared in .eslintrc.json as `local/no-silent-catch`, and that file is DEAD CONFIG — .eslintrc.cjs wins ESLint 8 precedence and declares neither the `local` plugin nor the rule, so `npx eslint --print-config src/lib/logger.ts` resolves with zero `local/*` rules. The rule's ONLY enforcement since 2026-04-03 has been Gate 2's explicit `--rulesdir` run over `pages/api`, i.e. 77 of the 1443 findings in the repo; src/ — which CLAUDE.md's zero-tolerance "no empty catch blocks" nominally covers — was never scanned. Measured on a clean tree of this branch (master 7ad8b7a3a) via scripts/silent-catch-ratchet.mjs: src 1192 (70 of them in test files, which .eslintrc.cjs lints and so are counted), pages non-api 174, pages/api 77. All pre-existing, none PR-introduced. Set AT the measured value so the gate ratchets down rather than blocking every PR; do not fold these into one number — see the pages/ note below for why per-scope is the shape here.
# 2026-08-22: NEW baseline MAX_UNTHEMED_LIGHT_SURFACES, introduced with the
# `no-unthemed-light-surface` rule (Gate 2f). First measured at 4, all of them in
# src/modules/fleet/operations/web/MapAttentionPanel.tsx — the panel that shipped
# to production at 1.04:1 contrast and started this exercise — whose fix was in
# flight on a separate branch and deliberately not duplicated here.
# 2026-08-23: that fix is now on master, so re-measured on this branch rebased
# onto master (1b985548f): 0 findings across 2112 linted .tsx files. Set to 0,
# which is the target; this gate is not a debt ratchet, it starts clean and any
# new finding is a regression.
#
# The gate asserts the linted FILE COUNT as well as the finding count. A scan
# that collapses — a moved directory, a bad --ext, a --rulesdir that fails to
# load — reports zero findings and is indistinguishable from a clean repo. That
# exact false green is what made `no-silent-catch` inert for two months.
#
# Why pages/ gets its OWN pair rather than folding into MAX_LINT_WARNINGS=1301:
# a combined number makes src and pages debt fungible. Paying down 100 pages
# warnings would silently buy headroom for 100 new src warnings, and the 186
# above took eight ratchet steps to earn. Gate 2 already scores pages/api under
# its own separate baseline, so per-scope numbers are the established shape here.
#
# KNOWN GAP, accepted deliberately: scripts/deploy-local-main.sh gates deploys on
# `npm run lint` (src) only — it is NOT extended to pages/. Every deploy ships
# origin/master, which the CI gate above already blocks, so the deploy check is a
# second line of defence rather than the primary one; extending it would add a
# second lint run to every production deploy. If that reasoning ever stops
# holding — e.g. deploys start coming from somewhere CI has not gated — the deploy
# script needs MAX_PAGES_LINT_* literals beside its existing ones.
# =============================================================================

# ESLint warnings from `npm run lint` (`eslint src`).
MAX_LINT_WARNINGS=186

# ESLint errors from `npm run lint`. Hard zero — never raise this.
MAX_LINT_ERRORS=0

# ESLint warnings from `npm run lint:pages` (`eslint pages`).
MAX_PAGES_LINT_WARNINGS=1115

# ESLint errors from `npm run lint:pages`. Hard zero — never raise this.
MAX_PAGES_LINT_ERRORS=0

# `no-silent-catch` findings across pages/api (catch blocks that swallow).
# Scored by scripts/silent-catch-ratchet.mjs, which also carries the two scopes
# below. This key keeps its name and its eight-step provenance log above.
MAX_SILENT_CATCHES=78

# `no-silent-catch` findings across pages/ EXCLUDING pages/api (page components).
# 2026-08-22: first measured at 174, re-measured at 175 after rebasing onto a
# master that had gained 18 commits. The extra one arrived through a merge that
# landed BEFORE this gate existed, so nothing could have stopped it — which is
# the argument for the gate, not against the number. Ratchet it down.
MAX_PAGES_OTHER_SILENT_CATCHES=175

# `no-silent-catch` findings across src/. Never gated before 2026-08-22.
# Same story: first measured at 1192, re-measured at 1193 on the same rebase.
MAX_SRC_SILENT_CATCHES=1193
# `no-unthemed-light-surface` findings across src/ + pages/ (*.tsx): a
# hard-coded light background with neither a dark: variant nor a paired
# dark-safe text colour, which renders light-on-light in dark mode.
# Currently clean. Any increase is a new defect, not debt — fix the code.
MAX_UNTHEMED_LIGHT_SURFACES=0
